## Medium tasks

### Is there a difference in 'order_hour_of_day' distributions on Wednesdays and Saturdays? Plot the histograms for both days on the same plot and describe the differences that you see.
orders_wed = orders[orders['order_dow'] == 3]
orders_sat = orders[orders['order_dow'] == 6]
orders_wed = orders_wed['order_hour_of_day'].value_counts().sort_index()
orders_sat = orders_sat['order_hour_of_day'].value_counts().sort_index()
combined_df = pd.concat([orders_wed, orders_sat], axis = 'columns')
combined_df.columns = ['Wednesday', 'Saturday']
combined_df
plt.figure(figsize=(10, 6))

plt.bar(combined_df.index - 0.2, combined_df['Wednesday'], width=0.4, label='Wednesday', color='blue', alpha=0.7)
plt.bar(combined_df.index + 0.2, combined_df['Saturday'], width=0.4, label='Saturday', color='orange', alpha=0.7)

plt.title('Comparison of Order Distribution by Hour')
plt.xlabel('Hour of Day')
plt.ylabel('Number of Orders')
plt.xticks(combined_df.index, rotation=60)
plt.legend()

plt.tight_layout()
plt.show()

Distributions look quite similar, but on Wednesdays we can see two peaks - on 10-11AM and 3-4PM, - and some decrease in between, while on Saturdays this timeframe between 11AM and 2PM is a peak.


